messages:
ana_docs: Pushed a docs PR that bundles a short migration checklist + SDK compatibility snippet for usage tiers, plus a sample Grafana alias query. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4281 :seedling:
kevin_devex: nice. can you paste the SDK snippet and the checklist items here so I can quick-review before diving into the PR?
sam_eng: heads-up: telemetry metric names changed in infra last sprint from `redwood.rate.limit` -> `redwood.rate_limit`. we should recommend an alias strategy for Grafana until customers fully migrate.
nana_docs: snippet (JS):
```js
// New method signature (stable)
const tiers = await sdk.fetchUsageTiers({ projectId: 'proj_123' });
// Stable response shape:
// { id: 'tier_free', name: 'Free', allocation_tokens: 50000, burst_window: 60 }
console.log(tiers);

// Temporary compatibility helper (internal flag; documented for migration)
const oldShape = await sdk.fetchUsageTiers({ projectId: 'proj_123', compat: true });
// oldShape returns legacy keys for a limited grace period
```
kevin_devex: two tiny suggestions: show a TypeScript example too and call out that `compat` is internal and only available for managed customers during the 2-week window.
sam_eng: also add a note about metrics: include the new metric name and an example alias rule so dashboards keep rendering historical panels.
nana_docs: added TS snippet and alias example. TS example: ```ts
const tiers = await sdk.fetchUsageTiers({ projectId: 'proj_123' }) as Array<{id: string; name: string; allocation_tokens: number; burst_window: number}>;
```
nana_docs: grafana alias / PromQL example I added: ```promql
avg_over_time(redwood_rate_limit{project="proj_123"}[30d])
# or use recording rule to map old metric
# record: redwood_rate_limit_alias
# expr: redwood_rate_limit OR redwood_rate.limit
```
ci-bot: docs build succeeded for PR 4281 44d  (lint: 0 warnings, 1 suggestion)
kevin_devex: LGTM. one editorial nit: the checklist item "Update any saved dashboards" should say "Review and update" so we're not telling customers to take immediate action. change that and I'll approve.
nana_docs: changed wording to "Review and update saved dashboards; consider adding a recording rule/alias for historical continuity." Added a short paragraph under "Migration windows" explaining the 2-week compat flag is temporary and only for customers on managed private deployments.
doc-bot: Note: added docs metadata tag `migration-guides` and bumped TOC.
nana_docs: thanks all — merging once CI green and changelog entry added under docs. :shipit:
